    "rules": [
      {
        "severity": "required",
        "text": "Keep copper, tracks, vias and other parts out of the antenna zone: the 28.5 mm wide, 11.5 mm deep area beyond the module's antenna end, drawn as part of the footprint's courtyard. Put the antenna end at, or just past, the board edge.",
        "basis": "convention"
      },
      {
        "severity": "required",
        "text": "Do not place a ground plane or copper under the antenna part of the module on any layer.",
        "basis": "convention"
      },
      {
        "severity": "recommended",
        "text": "The 10 uF and 0.1 uF decoupling capacitors sit at the module's 3V3 pin, on the side away from the antenna.",
        "basis": "convention"
      },
      {
        "severity": "info",
        "text": "Partly routed: the 0.1 uF decoupling capacitor at the 3V3 pin, the module's ground pin and the EN pull-up and capacitor are routed on the front layer. The rest is positioned and left as a ratsnest (including the 10 uF capacitor: put it within a few millimetres of the 3V3 pin). Route it yourself, with ground pour under and around the module body except at the antenna.",
        "basis": "convention"
      }
    ],
